<?php
/**
 * @var \Ahy\PDPRevamp\Block\Adminhtml\Attribute\Edit\Options\TwoColor $block
 *
 * "Add Swatch" here creates a brand-new attribute option exactly the way the
 * native "Manage Swatch" grid's own "Add Swatch" button does - it does NOT
 * introduce any new save logic. A new row's label/color/default fields are
 * named optionvisual[value][...] / swatchvisual[value][...] / defaultvisual[],
 * the exact same POST arrays Magento_Swatches' own EavAttribute plugin
 * already reads on save (see vendor/magento/module-swatches/Model/Plugin/
 * EavAttribute.php). That plugin copies "optionvisual" into the generic
 * "option" array Magento's core attribute-option save
 * (_updateAttributeOption(), module-eav) processes: any key that isn't
 * numeric is always treated as new and gets inserted with a real option_id,
 * before the swatch value is attached to it. Magento_Swatches' own
 * determineSwatchType() only checks the first character of the combined
 * value ("#" or "/"), so our "hex1,hex2" / "path1,path2" / mixed pairs are
 * accepted and stored exactly like AI-resolved pairs are. Temp keys are
 * prefixed (non-numeric) so is_numeric() on them is always false,
 * guaranteeing they're never mistaken for a real existing option_id.
 * defaultvisual[] is the exact same radio group name the native grid's own
 * rows use, so marking a brand-new two-color option as default correctly
 * competes with every other option on the page, native or not.
 *
 * Each color half's actual value (hex OR an uploaded image's relative path)
 * lives in a plain hidden input - the source of truth submitted on save.
 * The visible <input type="color"> next to it is transient scratch space
 * only: browsers reject a non-hex value in a color input outright, so it
 * can't hold an image path itself. "Upload a file" posts directly to
 * Magento_Swatches' own vendor/magento/module-swatches/Controller/Adminhtml/
 * Iframe/Show.php (getUploadUrl()) - the exact endpoint the native "Manage
 * Swatch" grid's own upload option uses - which moves the file to permanent
 * storage and returns its relative path immediately, so nothing extra is
 * needed on save for an uploaded image to become the option's swatch value.
 *
 * Existing (already-paired) rows' Admin/store-view label fields are
 * editable here too, but deliberately NOT under the native grid's own
 * "optionvisual[value][...]" name - that row is intentionally left in place
 * in "Manage Swatch" (not removed), and reusing its field name would mean
 * whichever of the two renders last on the page silently wins on save,
 * discarding an edit made in the other. Ours instead submits under its own
 * "ahy_two_color_swatch[<id>][label][<store_id>]" name and is written
 * directly via NativeColorSwatch::saveOptionLabel() in SaveTwoColorSwatch -
 * a fully independent read/write path, so editing one can never clobber
 * the other.
 */
$rows = $block->getTwoColorRows();
$stores = $block->getStoreViews();
$mediaBaseUrl = $block->getSwatchMediaBaseUrl();

/**
 * @param string $value hex ("#RRGGBB") or an uploaded image's relative path
 */
$faceStyle = static function (string $value) use ($block, $mediaBaseUrl): string {
    if ($block->isImagePath($value)) {
        return 'background-image: url(\'' . $mediaBaseUrl . $value . '\'); '
            . 'background-size: cover; background-position: center;';
    }

    return 'background-color: ' . $value . ';';
};
